<a name="Intro"></a>
<h1>Introduction</h1>

<h3> About the example </h3>
This example solves one system with CB-GMRES repeatedly, over a list of
storage precisions and a list of restart ratios, and reports the iteration
count, the solve time and the relative residual of each combination:

@code{.sh}
cb-gmres-sweep [executor] [matrix.mtx] [krylov_dim] [restart_ratios] [storage]
@endcode

Every combination runs in one process, the matrix being parsed once and reused,
since parsing a large matrix costs more than solving with it. A restart ratio
of zero restarts after @p krylov_dim steps, and a positive one ends a cycle
once the correction has reduced the residual by that factor, with
@p krylov_dim acting only as a cap on the basis.

The right-hand side, the stopping tolerance, the iteration cap, the number of
repetitions, the preconditioner and the per-cycle log are selected through
environment variables; run with @p --help for the list.
